  <!-- Additive IK scene for the Marvin Tianji CCS-696 dual 7-DOF arm.

       This file is the SAME arm kinematic tree as
       sim_infra/assets/robots/tianji_marvin_ccs_696/tianji_marvin_CCS.xml
       (which already has the corrected joint axes per urdf_conversion_bug.md),
       with three additions required by the mink-IK pipeline:

         1. `left_wrist` / `right_wrist` EE sites at the tool flange. The site
            pose matches the one used in the existing sim_infra collision XML
            (`pos="0 -0.095 0" xyaxes="0 0 1 -1 0 0"` on Link7).
         2. Per-link collision capsules `{side}_link{i}_col` for i ∈ 1..7,
            named exactly so sim_infra/grill_sim_infra/teleop/ik_mink.py's
            `_build_collision_limit` (look up by name at ik_mink.py:115-131)
            finds them. Sizes copied from
            DexTele/robots/tianji/tianji_marvin_CCS_real_limit_wuji_sim_infra_col.xml.
         3. `pillar_geom` for arm-vs-pillar collision avoidance.

       Nothing in the joint/body tree changes — FK against Marvin_Kine.fk()
       must still agree to sub-mm per scripts/verify_mjcf_vs_sdk.py.

       Meshes live under the sim_infra tree; this file references them via
       `meshdir` set at load time (see
       MarvinMinkIK.__init__ in marvin_mink_adapter.py). -->

